---

# 10. Governance

The Trading Intelligence Platform shall be governed through:

* Project Master Library (PML).
* Architecture Decision Records (ADR).
* Version-controlled documentation.
* Git-based source control.
* Peer review.
* Automated testing.
* Release approval workflow.

---

# 11. Deliverables

The project shall produce:

* Project Master Library.
* Enterprise architecture documentation.
* Technical design documentation.
* Production-ready MQL5 source code.
* Production-ready Python services.
* Database schema and migration scripts.
* Automated test suites.
* CI/CD pipelines.
* Deployment scripts.
* User and technical documentation.

---

# 12. Risks

Key project risks include:

* Architectural drift.
* Inconsistent coding practices.
* Scope expansion without governance.
* Insufficient automated testing.
* Security vulnerabilities.
* Technology dependency changes.
* Performance degradation as complexity grows.

These risks shall be actively managed through the governance processes defined in the PML.

---

# 13. Project Lifecycle

The project lifecycle is defined as:

1. Business Requirements
2. Enterprise Architecture
3. Technical Design
4. Project Master Library
5. Software Implementation
6. Testing & Verification
7. Deployment
8. Operations
9. Continuous Improvement

Progression between phases requires completion of the defined quality gates.

---

# 14. Authority

This Project Charter establishes the official objectives, governance, and direction of the Trading Intelligence Platform.

All contributors shall comply with this charter and with the standards defined throughout the Project Master Library.

Any deviation from this charter shall require formal review and approval through the project's governance process.

